  "query_preview": "/Thursday through Monday/...\nIssued 430 AM MDT MON AUG 24 2026\nAn upper level trough off the West Coast will push the monsoon \nmoisture south and east of our area. Height falls throughout the\nperiod will allow for a slight cooling trend. Temperatures will\nbe around 5 degrees above normal Thursday, before cooling to\nnear normal Friday and Saturday, and slightly below normal on\nSunday. Uncertainty begins to increase late this week, \nfollowing the lifting of the initial trough and associated \nfrontal passage as tropical activity in the Pacific enhances the\njet stream. Models do not handle the energy transfer well in\nthese situations so expect lots of changes in the far extended \nperiod.",
